He even cheated on a test
when he was a cadet.

264
00:11:32,734 --> 00:11:34,194
The kobayashi mar...

265
00:11:34,403 --> 00:11:35,070
The what?

266
00:11:35,279 --> 00:11:36,071
Kobayashi mar...

267
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,990
Kirk is a legend because of it.

268
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:41,618
Ko-kobayashi mar...

269
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:44,079
Sounds like something
you eat at benihana's.

270
00:11:44,288 --> 00:11:45,648
Have you ever been
to one of those?

271
00:11:45,706 --> 00:11:46,724
They make you sit
with strangers.

272
00:11:46,748 --> 00:11:47,958
It's crazy.

273
00:11:50,836 --> 00:11:52,921
Do you think a Spock
could become a kirk?

274
00:11:53,964 --> 00:11:55,340
Well, in my experience,

275
00:11:55,549 --> 00:11:57,551
most people stay
the miserable bastards they are

276
00:11:57,759 --> 00:11:58,886
their whole entire life.

277
00:11:59,094 --> 00:12:00,220
But...

278
00:12:00,721 --> 00:12:03,015
I have seen some folks change.

279
00:12:05,559 --> 00:12:06,559
Hmm.

280
00:12:08,812 --> 00:12:11,231
All right. Well, I'm gonna
go play with this train.

281
00:12:11,899 --> 00:12:12,899
You do that.

282
00:12:30,209 --> 00:12:30,834
Sheldon: Georgie?

283
00:12:31,126 --> 00:12:31,752
Go away.

284
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,253
I need to ask a favor.

285
00:12:33,462 --> 00:12:34,254
What?

286
00:12:34,463 --> 00:12:36,298
It's private. Can I come in?

287
00:12:37,007 --> 00:12:38,217
Come on.

288
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:44,598
What do you want?

289
00:12:45,182 --> 00:12:47,351
It occurs to me
you have something in common

290
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:48,644
with captain kirk.

291
00:12:48,852 --> 00:12:50,187
We both have cool hair?

292
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:51,395
In order to succeed,

293
00:12:51,563 --> 00:12:53,815
you both play fast and loose
with the rules.

294
00:12:54,524 --> 00:12:56,109
Yeah, I suppose we do.

295
00:12:56,318 --> 00:12:59,154
When you cheated on the math
test, what was your strategy?

296
00:12:59,905 --> 00:13:01,406
Well, I guess the most
important part

297
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:04,034
was not stepping on anything wet
before the test.

298
00:13:04,743 --> 00:13:05,827
And not getting an "a."

299
00:13:06,495 --> 00:13:07,788
Why wouldn't you want an "a"?

300
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:10,457
'Cause that would
raise suspicions.

301
00:13:10,707 --> 00:13:12,084
Who would believe I got an "a"?

302
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:13,669
Wow.

303
00:13:13,877 --> 00:13:15,170
Tell me more.

304
00:13:15,379 --> 00:13:17,547
Okay, when you're telling a lie,

305
00:13:17,756 --> 00:13:19,800
it's important to throw in
some details.

306
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:22,320
Like, when I was wanted to spend
the night at Ricky's house,

307
00:13:22,344 --> 00:13:24,972
and mom asked me if his mom
and dad were gonna be home,

308
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,180
I said, not only

309
00:13:26,265 --> 00:13:27,432
are they be gonna be home,

310
00:13:27,641 --> 00:13:28,681
his dad was gonna teach us

311
00:13:28,767 --> 00:13:30,894
how to cook Turkey legs
in the smoker.

312
00:13:31,103 --> 00:13:32,980
I like Turkey legs.
Were they good?

313
00:13:33,188 --> 00:13:35,357
There weren't any Turkey legs,
you dope.

314
00:13:35,691 --> 00:13:37,192
His parents were in Branson.

315
00:13:37,401 --> 00:13:40,237
That's incredible.
I totally believed you.

316
00:13:41,071 --> 00:13:42,071
Details.

317
00:13:42,114 --> 00:13:44,533
Now get out of here,
I got to finish reading this.

318
00:13:45,993 --> 00:13:48,704
Thank you, Georgie,
that was very helpful.

319
00:13:50,247 --> 00:13:51,498
Did you hear that?

320
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:52,499
What?

321
00:13:52,708 --> 00:13:53,893
Sounds like Georgie and Sheldon

322
00:13:53,917 --> 00:13:55,043
are getting along.

323
00:13:55,252 --> 00:13:56,252
Really?

324
00:13:56,837 --> 00:13:57,837
That can't be right.

325
00:13:58,005 --> 00:13:59,006
I just heard it.

326
00:13:59,172 --> 00:14:01,133
Maybe there's hope
for those two after all.

327
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,510
Or it's a sign of
the apocalypse.

328
00:14:03,719 --> 00:14:05,387
Honey, I'm-I'm watching this.

329
00:14:10,892 --> 00:14:12,311
So you'll have to
find someone else

330
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:14,354
to hold your ankles
in pe. Today.

331
00:14:14,563 --> 00:14:15,856
I'm sorry, what?

332
00:14:16,064 --> 00:14:17,304
I've suffered a terrible injury

333
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:18,859
and won't be able to attend.

334
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:20,067
What happened?

335
00:14:20,402 --> 00:14:21,486
See for yourself.

336
00:14:24,114 --> 00:14:27,409
"Dear coach Wilkins,
please excuse my son, Sheldon,

337
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:28,617
"from p.E.

338
00:14:28,994 --> 00:14:31,038
"He has experienced
a testicular hernia,

339
00:14:31,246 --> 00:14:33,874
"and needs to rest for the next
six to eight weeks.

340
00:14:34,082 --> 00:14:35,709
Sincerely, Mary Cooper."

341
00:14:37,878 --> 00:14:39,046
Testicular hernia?

342
00:14:39,254 --> 00:14:41,590
That's called details.

343
00:14:43,383 --> 00:14:45,177
Ooh, that's rough.

344
00:14:45,594 --> 00:14:46,219
Hmm.

345
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:47,137
How'd it happen?

346
00:14:47,346 --> 00:14:48,680
It's hard to say,

347
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:52,184
but some risk factors include:
Heavy lifting, a chronic cough

348
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:54,686
and repetitive straining
during bowel movements.

349
00:14:55,312 --> 00:14:56,396
I've been there.

350
00:14:56,605 --> 00:14:58,190
Hmm. All right.

351
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:01,568
Guess I'll see you in...
Six to eight weeks.

352
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:10,178
Adult Sheldon: I don't know
if other supervillains

353
00:15:10,202 --> 00:15:11,244
started their careers

354
00:15:11,453 --> 00:15:13,246
by getting out of re,

355
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:14,831
but that's where I began.

356
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:17,417
Emboldened by my faux hernia,

357
00:15:17,626 --> 00:15:20,504
I started taking books
out of the library...

358
00:15:21,296 --> 00:15:23,423
Without getting
the cards stamped.

359
00:15:23,632 --> 00:15:24,901
You didn't check
out those books.

360
00:15:24,925 --> 00:15:25,926
I know.

361
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:28,428
Before you judge me too harshly,

362
00:15:28,637 --> 00:15:30,680
I always brought them back
on time.

363
00:15:30,931 --> 00:15:33,558
I was a rule-breaker,
not a lunatic.

364
00:15:33,975 --> 00:15:36,686
But perhaps my most
satisfying transgression

365
00:15:36,895 --> 00:15:38,605
was duping my sister

366
00:15:38,814 --> 00:15:41,566
into relinquishing control
of the TV.

367
00:15:43,652 --> 00:15:44,652
Hello.

368
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:46,279
What's that for?

369
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:50,117
Oh, this? I was just digging
for money in meemaw's backyard.

370
00:15:50,534 --> 00:15:51,952
There's money there?

371
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,454
Oh, yes. I already
found 75 cents.

372
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:56,289
Who do you think left it?

373
00:15:57,499 --> 00:15:58,125
If I were to guess,

374
00:15:58,333 --> 00:16:00,210
I'd say pirates
with holes in their pockets.

375
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,546
Can I use your shovel?

376
00:16:03,422 --> 00:16:04,965
Be my guest.

377
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:07,509
Missy: Oh, baby,
I'm gonna be rich.

378
00:16:10,387 --> 00:16:13,640
Today, we're going to learn
about sir Isaac Newton.

379
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:15,433
Hello, old friend.

380
00:16:15,517 --> 00:16:17,161
One of the world's
greatest scientists...

381
00:16:21,773 --> 00:16:22,773
See you tomorrow, Wayne.

382
00:16:22,858 --> 00:16:24,401
You have a good one, George.

383
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:26,445
Hey, how's your son doing?

384
00:16:26,695 --> 00:16:27,695
Georgie?

385
00:16:27,863 --> 00:16:29,156
No, the smart one.

386
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:32,033
He's fine. Why?

387
00:16:32,242 --> 00:16:33,910
What about the hernia?

388
00:16:34,286 --> 00:16:35,286
What hernia?

389
00:16:35,454 --> 00:16:37,330
The one your wife said he had.

390
00:16:41,168 --> 00:16:42,752
Happened to me
while I was in the army.

391
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:46,173
I was in a bar in Georgia,
tried to lift up this big gal.

392
00:16:47,215 --> 00:16:49,050
Swear I could hear something
pop down there.

393
00:16:49,259 --> 00:16:50,594
Sheldon gave you this note?

394
00:16:50,802 --> 00:16:51,802
Yeah.

395
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:53,263
I didn't write this.

396
00:16:53,472 --> 00:16:54,472
You sure?

397
00:16:54,806 --> 00:16:55,825
Looks like your handwriting.

398
00:16:55,849 --> 00:16:57,452
It's got that little
swoopy thing going on.

399
00:16:57,476 --> 00:16:58,476
I didn't write it.

400
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:01,104
And I think I'd know
if my son had a hernia.

401
00:17:01,313 --> 00:17:04,232
So what, Sheldon forged a
letter to get out of re?

402
00:17:04,483 --> 00:17:05,692
Looks like it.

403
00:17:06,443 --> 00:17:07,443
How about that.

404
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,988
Don't be proud of him.

405
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,908
Can't help it. First time
he ever seemed like my kid.

406
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:15,243
Do you have any idea

407
00:17:15,452 --> 00:17:16,578
what's gotten into him?

408
00:17:18,455 --> 00:17:19,455
I might.

409
00:17:19,706 --> 00:17:20,790
Well?

410
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:23,126
Have you ever heard of...

411
00:17:24,127 --> 00:17:26,880
Mobokachi kaboom?

412
00:17:27,339 --> 00:17:28,048
Wait.

413
00:17:28,298 --> 00:17:30,675
Koshimaki Magoo.

414
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:32,928
Wait a minute,
I'm gonna get this.

415
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:37,891
"Dear professor proton,

416
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:39,726
"I would very much
like to meet you,

417
00:17:39,935 --> 00:17:42,521
"and I only have
three weeks to live.

418
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:45,232
"Please come visit me here
in medford, Texas.

419
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,900
"Sincerely, Sheldon Cooper.

420
00:17:47,108 --> 00:17:49,152
P.s. My meemaw makes
excellent brisket."

421
00:17:49,361 --> 00:17:50,028
Mary: Sheldon.

422
00:17:50,237 --> 00:17:51,821
Would you like
to explain this note?

423
00:17:54,241 --> 00:17:55,242
Well?

424
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,243
I was trying to be

425
00:17:56,451 --> 00:17:57,451
more like Georgie.

426
00:17:57,619 --> 00:17:58,912
That's a dumb idea.

427
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,748
We don't want Georgie
to be like Georgie.

428
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:05,460
Well, let me start by saying
how very sorry I am.

429
00:18:12,092 --> 00:18:13,802
Adult Sheldon:
Despite my explanation

430
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:16,388
that I was embracing
my inner kirk,

431
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:20,350
my mother had me make amends
for all my misdeeds.

432
00:18:20,642 --> 00:18:21,893
Starting in the library,

433
00:18:22,102 --> 00:18:25,146
where I had to reshelve
hundreds of books.

434
00:18:25,564 --> 00:18:27,899
Well, to be honest,
that one was a hoot.

435
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:32,571
The amends got worse when coach
Wilkins made me climb the rope.

436
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:34,823
Lacking any upper body strength,

437
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:38,326
I hung there like a salami
in a deli window.

438
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:42,205
And finally, I had to apologize
to my meemaw,

439
00:18:42,414 --> 00:18:46,543
who was an unfortunate victim
of my sister's treasure hunt.

